PyTorch 2.12.1 for Delta — RH9.6 / CPE 26.3 (CUDA 13.0, Python 3.12)

Built for the RH9.6 stack: cu130 wheels (CUDA 13.0 runtime), mpi4py linked
against cray-mpich 9.1.0, system libfabric 2.3.1 (Slingshot CXI). Runs on
driver 595.71.05 natively. Refuses to load on RH9.4 nodes — use
pytorch-conda/2.8 there.

For documentation and examples:
  https://docs.ncsa.illinois.edu/systems/delta/

Run setup-kernel prior to launching an OOD job.

Quick start (on a RH9.6 compute node):
  module load pytorch-conda/2.12
  conda activate base
  python -c "import torch; print(torch.cuda.is_available())"

CUDA extensions: CUDA_HOME comes from the default cudatoolkit module
(cudatoolkit/default -> 26.5_13.2 on RH9.6, nvcc 13.2).

Multi-node NCCL: the aws-ofi-nccl plugin is loaded automatically, so NCCL
routes over Slingshot CXI rather than falling back to TCP sockets.

